Support anywidget's descriptor API (`MimeBundleDescriptor`) (#8972)

anywidget has a descriptor-based API
([`MimeBundleDescriptor`](https://anywidget.dev/en/experimental/#mimebundle-descriptor))
that lets any Python class become a widget without subclassing
`anywidget.AnyWidget` or depending on ipywidgets (or traitlets).

These changes patch `comm.create_comm` to return `MarimoComm` instances
so descriptor-created comms broadcast through marimo's notification
system. On the output side, when `_repr_mimebundle_` returns a jupyter
widget-view mimebundle, the formatter reads `_esm` from the descriptor
and produces the same `<marimo-anywidget>` HTML that `mo.ui.anywidget()`
produces.

```python
from dataclasses import dataclass
from anywidget._descriptor import MimeBundleDescriptor
import psygnal

@psygnal.evented
@dataclass
class Counter:
    count: int = 0
    _repr_mimebundle_ = MimeBundleDescriptor(_esm="""
    export default {
      render({ model, el }) {
        let btn = document.createElement("button");
        btn.textContent = `count is ${model.get("count")}`;
        btn.onclick = () => {
          model.set("count", model.get("count") + 1);
          model.save_changes();
        };
        model.on("change:count", () => {
          btn.textContent = `count is ${model.get("count")}`;
        });
        el.appendChild(btn);
      }
    }
    """)

counter = Counter()
counter
```

```py
counter.count = 50 # updates UI using psygnal eventing
```

