## What

A new **Settings → Router** tab tunes the four routers: FreeAuto Fast, FreeAuto, FreeAuto Smart and BalanceAuto. You don't have to edit a rules file or the code.

- **Model order.** Each router gets an ordered list of models, at most 6 (4–5 recommended). The list replaces the `use` list of the main routes (`default`, `coding`, `plan-and-reasoning`, `ask-reasoning`) and goes to the front of the pool. Example: to make FreeAuto start with GLM-5.2 instead of Kimi K2.6, move GLM-5.2 to the top. **Use only these models** limits the pool to the list.
- **Advanced:**
  - per-route model lists, reasoning (quick, think or each model's default), reasoning effort, and size bounds (for example the 180k huge-context threshold);
  - classifier on/off and timeout, completion judge on/off and timeout;
  - failover timeouts, failures before benching, bench time, failovers per turn;
  - reminders per run, stalls and failed commands before escalating;
  - background (utility) models, sticky model, context margin.
- **BalanceAuto paid/free thresholds are deliberately not exposed**, as decided. `maxPaidCallsPerTurn` stays a rules-file setting.

## How

- **Storage:** `routerTuning` in global state, typed and normalized in `src/shared/router-tuning.ts`.
- **Layers:** `applyRouterTuning` (`src/sdk/router/router-tuning.ts`) lays the tuning over the rules (built-in defaults, then global file, then workspace file). It replaces only the fields it sets. Model ids go through the rules-file filter, so FreeAuto still drops paid ids.
- **Wiring:** `installRouter` gets a `tuning` getter (from `sdk-session-config-builder.ts`) and reads it on every routed call, so there is no restart or session rebuild. The tuned rules are memoized per rules object and stored map.
- **Escalation constants:** the hard-coded guard limits (6 failed commands, 8 reminders, 3 stalls) are now the rules files' `escalation` block. The seed render and normalize handle it, so untouched seeds refresh through their hash marker.
- **RPCs:** `ModelsService.getRouterSettings` and `setRouterTuning` carry a JSON view. For each profile it holds the rules-file defaults, the tuning, and the candidate models (BalanceAuto also lists the paid ones).
- **Rules link:** `pliny://free-auto-rules/<profile>` opens one profile's rules file.
- **Docs:** `docs/router-settings.md`, linked from `AGENTS.md` and both router docs.

## Tests

All of these pass locally:

- New tests:
  - `router-tuning.test.ts` (overlay, GLM-first routing, exclusive, per-route overrides, paid filtering, memo);
  - `shared/router-tuning.test.ts`;
  - `setRouterTuning.test.ts`;
  - router-integration tests (the next call follows a changed tuning; escalation limits are honored);
  - builder wiring test;
  - `RouterSettingsSection.test.tsx`;
  - escalation parse in `router-rules.test.ts`.
- Suites: `bun run check-types`, `bun run lint`, `test:discovery`, `test:vitest` (2195 passed), `test:webview` (738 passed), knip `--production`, `check:docs`.

**Not done:** a manual dev-host check of the Router tab.

Pre-release: https://github.com/lgiaccar/PlinyCode/releases/tag/release_0.2.4-test.5

## Why

The History generation flow board (`/history/flow/:jobId`) had five problems:

- It often opened at 16% zoom as two narrow columns of tiny cards.
- Prompt cards showed only the pose line, never the prompt.
- It had no model, settings or analysis information.
- It showed **no input photos** for cloned or Studio-started catalog shoots. Live example: `job_1e8598b8…`, where the page had 12 nodes, 0 inputs and only prompt→image edges. Its work item's `planning_assets` rows are all role `generated`, and the session's 8 real references were never read.
- Its prompt card held a 16px canvas card inside a page that also had its own header.

This PR redesigns the board after the shared node-editor reference (grouped lanes, image cards with reference thumbnails, a text handle, a `Run` pill and a settings bar) and fixes the missing inputs.

## What changed

**Board (`CatalogPoseFlow.tsx`, `catalogPoseFlow.css`)**
- **Lanes:** four grouped lanes, Input → Product analysis → Prompting → Output images (3 × 2 grid). A lane can be dragged by its title.
- **Output card:**
  - the image, with a verdict chip (`DNA 95%`, `Needs review`, `Generating`, `Failed`);
  - thumbnails of the photos that fed it;
  - the change note and a **Run** pill. Still disabled until a note is typed; the paid-generation tooltip and placeholder are unchanged.
  - a version menu;
  - a settings bar with model, aspect, size, quality, download and More (copy link, full prompt, open full size).
- **Prompt card:** the full stored prompt (scrollable) and `@front` / `@model face` chips for the photos the pose used. The full-prompt dialog has **Copy**.
- **Analysis card:** model, thinking level, fallbacks, product facts, the six-pose plan with adopted reference postures, and the analysis and Product DNA versions.
- **Header:** SKU, status, analysis model, image model, settings, poses done and cost.
- **Viewport:**
  - opens fitted to the screen; when that would be unreadable (on a phone), it opens at the top-left at 42%;
  - only the user's own pans and zooms are saved;
  - layout key `v2`, so the old 16% viewports are dropped; old notes are still read.
- **States:** skeleton loading board, opacity fade-ins (no transforms, so handle positions stay correct), a progress bar while generating, failed and expired-link states.
- **Node type names:** prefixed `cpf-*`. React Flow's stylesheet styles its built-in `input` and `output` node wrappers, which outlined every card.

**Data**
- `catalogProduction.ts`: `getCatalogWorkflowDetail` now also returns:
  - `sessionReferences`, signed by `signedSessionReferences`; a foreign path keeps its stored URL instead of failing the board;
  - each pose group's `qa` from `poseGroupQa`; it is null while a re-generation runs.
- `OperationalWorkflowView`: prefers the session photos (what the generator received), with QA verdicts and per-pose settings.
- New `flowSummary.ts` builds the header and analysis summary from `session_data` and the job row.
- `formatModelName` moved to `src/lib/modelLabels.ts`, shared with History; History's behaviour is unchanged.
- `boardFromGenerationData` exports `referencesFromSession` and `adoptedPostures`, and returns the summary, settings and QA per pose.
- `GenerationFlowPage`: the duplicate header is gone; Retry re-fetches instead of reloading the page; action errors show above the board.
- `errors.ts`: three side-effect-free reads may retry once after a gateway cut: `history.generationFlow.get`, `studio.loadSession` and `jobs.downloadAsset`. Mutations stay excluded.
- Inter font added; it is used only inside the board.
- Studio: the live progress card of a queued shoot links to its flow board (**Watch generation flow**).

## Tests

- New `flow_board.test.ts`, added to **both** lists (`package.json` and `deploy-cloud-run.yml`). It covers:
  - the summary;
  - the verdict order;
  - session references and postures;
  - the trace board (settings, DNA, no verdict without an image);
  - path highlighting;
  - signing with Supabase, Firebase and a foreign path;
  - `poseGroupQa` while busy;
  - the shared model labels.
- `entrypoint_source.test.ts`: prefixed node types, viewport saved only on user moves, session inputs preferred, Retry without reload.
- `invoke_error_message.test.ts`: the three reads are retryable; mutations are still not.
- Results:
  - `test:catalog-workflow`: 440 and 51+1 passed;
  - `deno check --frozen supabase/functions/app-api/index.ts`: passes;
  - `npx tsc -b`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`: pass;
  - `node --test src/features/history/generation-flow/flowLinks.test.ts`: 11/11.
- Manual, in the local `/flow-example` board at 1600×900 and 375×812:
  - the layout fits at 60%;
  - Run is disabled with the tooltip until a note is typed, then enabled;
  - the note is saved;
  - clicking Pose 1 lights its 8 path edges;
  - a phone opens at the inputs.

## After merge

- Open live flow boards for a Studio (trace) job and a catalog-workflow job and confirm inputs, analysis, prompts and verdicts.
- Run one shoot end to end and view it on the board.

